 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gain against current and temperature",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "With VCE = 10 V the typical gain is close to 200 at 25 °C and 300 at 100 °C at 1 mA, and stays nearly level up to several hundred milliamps (about 196 and 283 at 550 to 600 mA). Above that it drops steeply, ending near 166 at 100 °C and 178 at 25 °C at 1 A (Fig.2). The guaranteed minimum falls from 100 at 250 mA to 60 at 500 mA and 20 at 1000 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Saturation",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Driven with IC = 10 × IB, VCE(sat) is about 25 mV (25 °C) and 27 mV (100 °C) at 1 mA, lowest near 19 to 21 mV around 8 mA, and rises to about 260 mV and 290 mV at 1 A (Fig.3). VBE(sat) at the same drive runs from about 575 mV (25 °C) and 424 mV (100 °C) at 1 mA to about 935 mV and 852 mV at 1 A (Fig.4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Base-emitter voltage",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At VCE = 5 V a collector current of 1 mA needs about 404 mV on the base at 100 °C and 569 mV at -25 °C; 1 A needs about 716 mV and 827 mV (Fig.5)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At 1 MHz the input capacitance Cib falls from about 196 pF at 0.1 V reverse bias to about 90 pF at 8 V, and the output capacitance Cob from about 34 pF at 0.1 V to about 7 pF at 20 V (Fig.6)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The SOT-23 body is molded in a compound rated UL 94V-0, RoHS compliant and halogen-free. The leads are solder plated and pass the MIL-STD-750 Method 2026 solderability test. Moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 to J-STD-020, for lead-free reflow peaking at 260 °C. The part is specified for low equivalent on-resistance."
  }
 ],
